  "expertPathWrong": "The path must start with /",
  "helpKeepaliveTitle": "Keepalive",
  "helpKeepaliveBody": "An idle tunnel sometimes gets closed: the server counts the session as unneeded, and a mobile network can freeze the connection quietly. Keepalive sends a signal on an idle session, so it stays alive.\nInterval: the engine takes a random number from the value you set to four times that value, so with 60 seconds the ping goes every 60..240 seconds.\nSignal: a session check (a light request; the server counts it as a request and keeps the tunnel) or an HTTP/2 PING frame (what browsers send, but the server does not count it as a request, so it does not hold the tunnel).\nSession lifetime: how many seconds the session lives without a signal. 0 means: as long as the server keeps it.",
  "helpXhttpTitle": "XHTTP",
  "helpXhttpBody": "Usually the tunnel talks to the server with CONNECT requests. In the XHTTP mode every connection of an app carries a pair of requests: GET down and POST up, and the destination address rides inside the body. On the wire these are ordinary HTTP requests, so the transport can go through a CDN and it survives a broken connection better.\nThe mode is not finished yet: there is no session resume after a break, no acknowledgements and no body encryption yet. The live servers do not have it, turn it on only against the lab.",
  "expertSettingsWrong": "Check the values in the expert settings"
}
